Theorem VF-4: Layer 4 FIP certification — Certified iff zero unmatched alloc/dealloc in realized IR

  Preconditions:
    - VF-4 governs the Layer-4 FIP-certification verifier per Annex E §AIMS VF-4: "proves FipContract::Certified functions have zero unmatched
      alloc/dealloc. Failures wrapped as FipStructural." Restated by sec-5 IC-6:
      "FipContract::Certified iff zero unmatched alloc/dealloc in realized IR."
    - VF-4's concrete shape is ArcFunction x FipContract -> Result ()
      (List FipVerificationError) per
      aims-proof/proofs/01-verification/Verification.proof. Failures are wrapped
      as VerifyError::FipStructural by the pipeline runner. Discharged here
      against the sec-01 Verification.proof sorry obligation.
    - This is the alloc-balance analogue of the sec-08 RC-balance ledger: a
      function's allocation lifecycle is a sequence of AllocEvents; the verifier
      computes (allocs - deallocs) and asserts a Certified function balances to
      net 0 (every allocation matched by an in-place reuse or a paired
      deallocation).
    - Shipped verifier site:
        * compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/verify/fip.rs
          verify_fip_contract proves Certified functions have zero unmatched
          alloc/dealloc in the realized IR.
    - depends-on sec-06: IC-6 FipContract soundness is load-bearing; the
      provisional FipContract assigned during interprocedural extraction is
      verified or downgraded here (Step 5a) against the realized IR.

  Soundness property:
    Forall realized ArcFunction F with FipContract claim:

      (P1) Certification iff balance: F is FipContract::Certified IFF F's
           realized IR has zero unmatched allocations — the allocation ledger
           (allocs created minus deallocations + in-place reuses) nets 0. A
           function with an unmatched allocation (net != 0) MUST NOT be
           Certified.

      (P2) Reuse counts as matching: a Reset+Reuse pair (the dying allocation
           reused IN PLACE for a fresh same-type allocation) is allocation-
           neutral (net 0) — this is the FIP win, allocation-free via reuse. A
           pure FIP function with no allocations also nets 0.

    VF-4 is the FIP layer: it proves the alloc-balance the FipContract claims.
    A Certified function that allocates without freeing (net > 0) is a leak
    relative to the contract; one that frees more than it allocates (net < 0)
    is a double-free relative to the contract. Either disqualifies certification.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the rc_counting engine via per-instruction
    allocation-delta arithmetic + balance-equation witness construction (per
    the proof-checker design sec-Engine-per-Category-Inventory VF row; the foundational-axiom policy
    sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape — structural induction on the
    instruction list, allocation-delta arithmetic over integers; forbids
    classical existence of a balancing witness — the witness is constructed).

    Part (P1/P2) — FIP alloc-balance ledger:

      A function's allocation lifecycle is modeled as an ordered AllocEvent
      sequence (Alloc = +1, Dealloc = -1, ReuseInPlace = 0); the verifier
      computes net = (allocs) - (deallocs) and asserts net = 0 for every
      Certified function. Discharged cases:
        alloc_matched_dealloc_certified — alloc, matching dealloc -> net 0.
        reuse_in_place_certified — a Reset+Reuse pair (allocation-free
                                          via in-place reuse) -> net 0.
        mixed_balanced_certified — balanced alloc/dealloc pairs + an
                                          in-place reuse -> net 0.
        no_allocations_certified — a pure FIP function, empty ledger
                                          -> net 0.

    Negative-direction witnesses (the balance check has teeth — an unbalanced
    function is REJECTED for certification):
      NEG_unmatched_alloc_not_certified — an allocation with no paired dealloc
                                          and no reuse: net = +1 (a leak relative
                                          to the contract). NOT Certified.
      NEG_unmatched_dealloc_not_certified — more deallocations than allocations:
                                          net = -1 (a double-free relative to the
                                          contract). NOT Certified.
      Coverage gate: 6 ledger cases (4 Certified net-0 + 2 non-certified
      witnesses).

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY — section_09::verify_vf4_fip_certification;
        per-instruction allocation-delta arithmetic over the FIP balance ledger;
        emits Fail on a certification/balance mismatch)
      structural_induction (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the
        coverage-manifest VF row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      interprocedural_summary (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_09 rc_counting engine discharges VF-4 via the FIP alloc-balance ledger (Certified iff zero unmatched alloc/dealloc): 4 Certified net-0 lifecycles (alloc+dealloc, Reset+Reuse in-place, mixed balanced, empty) plus 2 non-certified negative-direction witnesses (unmatched alloc = leak, unmatched dealloc = double-free), grounded in the shipped compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/verify/fip.rs verify_fip_contract certification verifier
